# MediaMitigator Architecture Rules

## App Pattern: Wizard
- Main window hosts a QStackedWidget — one widget per step
- Steps are numbered 1-8, navigation via Next/Back/Cancel
- Each step is a self-contained QWidget subclass in gui/steps/
- Steps communicate state via a shared WizardState dataclass passed by reference
- No step directly imports another step

## Step Definitions
1. DriveSelectionStep — select drives to scan
2. InitialScanStep — scan progress + results summary
3. DestinationStep — browse/create destination folder
4. FolderReviewStep — hierarchical tree of folders to transfer
5. TransferSettingsStep — exclusions, empty folder behavior, notifications
6. PreTransferStep — time estimate, phase decision
7. ProgressStep — live transfer progress
8. ReportStep — final summary, errors, duplicates, navigation

## Threading Model
- Scanner runs in ScanWorker(QThread)
- Transfer runs in TransferWorker(QThread)
- Workers emit signals: progress_updated, item_completed, error_occurred, phase_completed, transfer_complete
- GUI only connects to signals — never calls worker methods directly
- Workers check a cancellation_event (threading.Event) every iteration to support clean cancellation

## Core Module Responsibilities
- scanner.py: walk drives, identify media files, build FolderNode tree
- analyzer.py: determine destination paths, estimate transfer time, calculate phases
- transfer_engine.py: execute copy-verify-delete, emit progress signals
- duplicate_detector.py: detect and route duplicates
- date_resolver.py: EXIF → creation date fallback, majority year logic
- phase_manager.py: split transfer into phases, manage auto-queue

## State Management
- WizardState is the single source of truth passed through all steps
- Settings persisted to: %APPDATA%/MediaMitigator/settings.json
- Session state (for resume) saved to: %APPDATA%/MediaMitigator/session_state.json
- Transfer logs saved to: logs/transfer_<timestamp>.log
- Reports saved to: reports/report_<timestamp>.html

## UI/UX Rules
- Dark theme using QDarkStyle or custom QPalette
- Step indicator/breadcrumb always visible at top of window
- Cancel button always accessible during long operations
- Progress bars for both overall and current-item progress
- Errors shown inline in a collapsible error panel, never as popups
- All destructive actions require visual confirmation indicator (not modal popup — use inline warning banner)
- Folder tree uses QTreeWidget with checkboxes, size column, file count column, and destination preview column
- Right-click on folder node → "Open in Explorer" option

## Notification System
- Use plyer for Windows toast notifications
- Notify on: phase complete, full transfer complete, errors exceeding threshold (>10 errors)
- Email notifications optional — configured in settings with SMTP host/port/credentials stored in settings.json (not hardcoded)
- Notification preference configurable in TransferSettingsStep

